children.text:
Take each child c in the list in order and do three things:

step the counter k[0] one forward, so every child under this top node gets its own number, however deep it sits;

set c["id"] = the top node id, a dot, and that number — for example F03.7;

when c has children of its own, call walk on them, so the whole tree below the top node gets ids from the same counter.
